**Relevant behavior:** `toggle_flag()` already toggles flags, and `reveal()` already skips flagged or previously revealed cells. In `game.py`, a mine hit ends the game before the win check. The issue was `won()`: counting revealed cells doesn’t directly verify that every non-mine cell was revealed.

**Change:** Updated only [board.py](board.py#L60) so victory requires every non-mine cell to be in `revealed`:

```python
def won(self):
    return all(
        (r, c) in self.revealed
        for r in range(self.rows)
        for c in range(self.cols)
        if (r, c) not in self.mines
    )
```

